{"id":14,"event":"agent","data":{"type":"text_delta","delta":"\n<od-done key=\"bd6f04728b04c0b8\"/>\n**Build “Intersection Reflex,” a tiny traffic-safety game.**\n\nA scene presents a structured situation—signal state, pedestrian, nearby vehicle, and road condition. Ollaya chooses from a bounded set of semantic actions such as **go, yield, stop,** or **request review**. A simple 2D intersection then plays out the result.\n\nThe player earns progress for safe decisions, not for speed alone. Unfamiliar or ambiguous scenes can trigger a visible System 2 escalation; after a policy update, replay the same scene to show how behavior changed.\n\nThis makes the System 1 loop tangible: **state → action probabilities → selected behavior → outcome**, without suggesting Ollaya directly controls vehicle physics.\n\n**Small first version:** one intersection, four actions, a handful of scenarios, and a decision trace showing probabilities and policy version."},"timestamp":1790819205480}
